  "body": "Second step of the maintainer's decision of 2026-11-11 to replace truck with solidcore (first step: #916, the bench).\n\nWhat: `crates/app`'s STEP import (`crates/app/src/geometry/import/step*.rs`) goes through the kernel seam's solidcore STEP importer; every import test, golden and fixture keeps its verdict or the change is listed and decided; then `truck-*` and `ruststep` leave `Cargo.toml` and `Cargo.lock` (which also ends the ruststep git pin - #909 closes with this), and truck's kernel role is retired as #27 says.\n\nBlocked on: #916 (the agreement bench must agree, and its tessellation answer decides how the mesh is made here).\n\nSafety floor: imported geometry is what every toolpath and gouge check is judged against. The unit handling (#306, #689), the chord caps (#689, #864), the reduced-fidelity flag (#864 / PR #911) and the corrupt-input laws must all hold on the new importer, each with its existing pin.\n\nStill open when this lands: the solidcore crates themselves are a git pin until upstream publishes them - a follow-up issue like #909 is filed then.\n\nPart of #27.\n\nDone means: no `truck-*` or `ruststep` package in `Cargo.lock`; the import suites, the STEP unit and chord suites and the release tier are green; IGES stays refused by name unless #27 says otherwise.\n",
